Same as lemaker-lcd7 with a 42.429 MHz pixel clock (about 50 Hz)

The LCD and HDMI share the PLL3 clock. HDMI sets it to 297 MHz in 1080p
and 720p, this pixel clock is derived from the same 297 MHz, so the LCD
does not flicker. Other HDMI modes change PLL3 and the LCD flickers again.
To keep HDMI at 1080p add to /boot/armbianEnv.txt:

	extraargs=video=HDMI-A-1:1920x1080@60
